            <ArticleTitle>Biceps pain as the presenting symptom of Parkinson disease: effective treatment with L-dopa.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>776-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Parkinson disease can present remarkably as shoulder pains that may long precede the clinical diagnosis. A case is presented in which, during a 2-year period, both lower biceps brachii became exquisitely painful, with both the pain and the &quot;frozen shoulders&quot; responding promptly to the initiation of L-dopa therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
